        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spline uses a CurveEvaluator to turn control points and parameters into an evaluated curve. The source includes Catmull–Rom, B-spline/de Boor, natural cubic spline, Hermite and Bézier evaluators. Their control-point semantics differ: interpolating splines pass through data points, while an approximating B-spline generally follows a control polygon without visiting every control point."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
            "Method",
            "Use",
            "Watch for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "cells": [
                "Catmull–Rom",
                "Smooth paths through samples",
                "Endpoint behavior and parameterization"
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                "B-spline",
                "Smooth controlled approximation",
                "Degree, knots and sufficient control points"
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
